      "writtenOn": "2026-06-30T07:32:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "```suggestion\n    \u003c!-- This map exists to stop the panel going fully black at low brightness.\n         Without a map the framework lets the brightness reach 0 (screen off).\n         With a map, the low end is pinned to the minimum backlight instead,\n         so the bottom panel always stays lit. --\u003e\n    \u003cscreenBrightnessMap\u003e\n        \u003cpoint\u003e\n            \u003cvalue\u003e0.0\u003c/value\u003e\n            \u003cnits\u003e2.0\u003c/nits\u003e\n        \u003c/point\u003e\n        \u003cpoint\u003e\n            \u003cvalue\u003e1.0\u003c/value\u003e\n            \u003cnits\u003e500.0\u003c/nits\u003e\n        \u003c/point\u003e\n    \u003c/screenBrightnessMap\u003e\n```\n\nThis can be simplified to the 2 point curve above. Any curve shaping is a no-op, and the nits are as well due to the lack of an ambient light sensor, but we need this to anchor the bottom panel and avoid blanking it at lower top display brightnesses\n\nThis\u0027ll probably become irrelevant with independent screen brightness",
      "revId": "a4d723f39ce2d1b909107b74ee6837096921428b",
      "serverId": "1ec6b3db-b2c1-4fa4-84a2-4c7efe89ba71"
